Seems like we're always complaining about loopholes, bugs, misfeatures,
whatever in this game that we spend too much time on... Anyway, for a
change of pace, I'll relate a case where I thought I had a neat trick
to "beat the system" but the good 'ol dev team had beat me to it....

Spoilers (sorta) discussed

We know that you can move from level 1 to deep in the dungeon and back
with cursed scrolls of teleportation and teleport control.  You can
also bring Fido with you if he's on a leash.

Unfortunately, once you have the Amulet in your possession, level
teleport doesn't work - forcing you to drag your butt out of the
dungeon with occasional reincarnations of you-know-who nipping
at your heels (unless you are clever....)

My brainstorm:  In a game I was playing, I located the Wiz and obtained
the amulet (over his objections).  Then I put it down, level teleported
back to where I had left my faithful mutt.  Slipped on a leash, level
teleported back into hell, and within a few moves, I had convinced my
leashed dog to pick up the Amulet.  Ah Hah!  Now I could level teleport
'cause I didn't have the Amulet.  And it worked...sort of...I indeed
level teleported back to 1, but Fido looked disoriented, the leash
slipped off, and.... dev team, my hats off to you guys on that one.


